<%- include('partials/head') %>
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A Hack Club YSWS · now transmitting</p>
        <p class="sponsor-credit">Supported by <strong>Arcade W</strong></p>
        <h1>Build your way <em>onto the air.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Learn amateur radio, build something real, document your progress, and ship projects to earn gear that takes you further.</p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/auth/login">Start with Hack Club</a>
          <a class="button button-ghost" href="#how">See the signal path</a>
        </div>
        <p class="microcopy">Open internationally · no previous radio experience needed</p>
      </div>
      <div class="signal-card" aria-label="A radio signal travelling from your project to the International Space Station">
        <div class="signal-topline"><span>LIVE PATH</span><span>145.990 → 437.800 MHz</span></div>
        <div class="orbit">
          <img src="/assets/ISS_picto.png" alt="International Space Station">
          <span class="orbit-ring ring-one"></span>
          <span class="orbit-ring ring-two"><span class="signal-orbit"><span class="signal-dot"></span></span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="signal-log">
          <span>PROJECT</span><b>→</b><span>CALLSIGN</span><b>→</b><span>ISS</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof-strip" aria-label="Program benefits">
    <div class="shell proof-grid">
      <div><strong>Covered</strong><span>exam and licence support</span></div>
      <div><strong>5 hertz / hour</strong><span>spent in the CQ shop</span></div>
      <div><strong>Real projects</strong><span>built by you</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell" id="how">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The signal path</p>
      <h2>From curious to callsign.</h2>
      <p>Turn an idea into a working radio project, share the journey, and get closer to going on air.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <article class="step-card"><span>01</span><h3>Make a project</h3><p>Build electronics or software that is directly related to ham radio. Studying by itself does not count.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><span>02</span><h3>Share your progress</h3><p>Document your project as it comes together with devlogs and photos from along the way.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><span>03</span><h3>Ship your project</h3><p>Finish your build and show us what you made.</p></article>
      <article class="step-card"><span>04</span><h3>Choose a prize</h3><p>Approved hours earn 5 hertz each. Use them for radios, receivers, build kits, or licence support.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reward-section" id="rewards">
    <div class="shell reward-layout">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Earn it, then get ready</p>
        <h2>The radio is a prize—not the quiz prize.</h2>
        <p>You earn enough hertz by shipping approved ham-radio projects. If you choose a transmitting radio, you then complete a short readiness check so we know you understand how to use it safely and are ready to work toward the real licence exam.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reward-cards">
        <article><span>RADIO</span><h3>Earn → check → fulfil</h3><p>Earn the hertz, choose the radio, complete the readiness check, and we’ll help get it to you.</p></article>
        <article><span>LICENCE</span><h3>Earn → grant → exam</h3><p>Licence funding is a shop prize issued as a grant through HCB. Costs and the local exam process vary, so higher-cost licences take more approved project time.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-dark" id="radio">
    <div class="shell split-feature">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The cool part</p>
        <h2>Yes, you can hear space.</h2>
        <p>The ISS cross-band repeater receives on 145.990 MHz FM with a 67 Hz tone and retransmits on 437.800 MHz FM. Start by listening; build a Yagi and the signal gets dramatically clearer.</p>
        <div class="frequency-grid">
          <div><small>UPLINK</small><strong>145.990</strong><span>MHz FM</span></div>
          <div><small>DOWNLINK</small><strong>437.800</strong><span>MHz FM</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="radio-stack">
        <img src="/assets/antenna_img.png" alt="Directional antenna">
        <div><strong>Antenna build</strong><span>20 hertz</span></div>
        <img src="/assets/radio_img.png" alt="Handheld radio">
        <div><strong>Handheld radio</strong><span>from 30 hertz</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell" id="safety">
    <div class="safety-card">
      <div class="safety-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</div>
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Listen first</p><h2>Transmit only when licensed.</h2><p>Receiving, owning, importing, and transmitting are treated differently around the world. You are responsible for following current local rules and must not transmit until you have the required licence and callsign.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your first contact starts here</p>
      <h2>Ready to call CQ?</h2>
      <a class="button button-light" href="/auth/login">Sign in with Hack Club</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
